<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina gets loan for copper smelter study.</title>
<headline>Argentina gets loan for copper smelter study.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina has received a loan for $484,700 from the U.S. Trade and Development Agency to fund a feasibility study of a $350 million copper smelter and refinery complex, the government said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The study will consider installing a smelter to process 400,000 tonnes a year of concentrates, producing 100,000 tonnes of refined copper, the Industry, Trade and Mining Secretariat said in a news release.</p>
<p>The complex's acid byproducts would probably be used for fertilizer production, the Secretiat said.</p>
<p>Argentina has attracted major interest from international copper mining companies in recent years. The $1 billion Bajo de la Alumbrera copper and gold mine is due to start production later this year.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
